Z||000013||grgoyl86||09-16-2001||10:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spiff:<BR><B>[QUOTE]Originally posted by Denny:<BR>[B] Why don't you connect with Bob Schlag and run with him? He lives near Dover.<P>We usually meet for breakfast at Zinn's Diner, then all Fierovan from there.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I may just do that and give Bob an E-Mail. I also have a friend that works at Silk City Diner up the road. Maybe I can get Bob to go there instead. That's if we Fierovan together. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah! Silk City works for me! Let's plan on that.<P>Hey Spiff, I usually go over Mt. Zion Hill and catch rte 30 there by the Galleria Mall. Maybe we can meet up there? I need to think about what time . . .<P><P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Schlag</B><BR><I>Mid Atlantic Fiero Owners Association</I><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieropride.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000014||grgoyl86||09-16-2001||10:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>I am planing on attending...that is if all goes well this weekend.<P>Looking at FieroPride.com...only 1 Fiero Class?  All modifieds grouped together?  Should be interesting!<P>Hopefully I can paint the car and get everything done before the show.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, one Fiero class, for stock Fieros. There is one class for other Modifieds, but the Fieros usually dominate this class. I expect it won't be long before owners of "other" modified cars will push to get us our own Mod class!  8^)<P>See ya there!<P><P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Schlag</B><BR><I>Mid Atlantic Fiero Owners Association</I><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieropride.com</A>||||reg||1
